WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.092 --> 00:00:16.901
The Mock Turtle sighed deeply and wiped his eyes with his flippers.

2
00:00:17.761 --> 00:00:19.683
He looked at Alice and tried to speak.

3
00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:22.104
But he started sobbing instead.

4
00:00:22.124 --> 00:00:25.866
"Don't worry," the Gryphon said to Alice.

5
00:00:25.886 --> 00:00:28.228
"He's always like this."

6
00:00:29.472 --> 00:00:33.394
The Mock Turtle soon recovered and began to explain the lobster dance.

7
00:00:34.255 --> 00:00:37.236
"You probably haven't ever lived under the sea."

8
00:00:37.256 --> 00:00:41.098
"No, I haven't," Alice said.

9
00:00:41.118 --> 00:00:45.421
"And perhaps you've never been introduced to a lobster."

10
00:00:46.301 --> 00:00:50.183
Alice started to say that she had eaten a lobster but stopped.

11
00:00:50.203 --> 00:00:56.567
"So you don't know how delightful a lobster dance is," the Mock Turtle said.

12
00:00:57.647 --> 00:00:58.648
Alice shook her head.

13
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.341
"No, I don't."

14
00:01:01.442 --> 00:01:03.264
The Gryphon joined the conversation.

15
00:01:03.284 --> 00:01:07.567
"First, you stand in a line along the seashore."

16
00:01:08.628 --> 00:01:11.070
"Two lines," the Mock Turtle corrected him.

17
00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:19.577
"Then, after you've cleared all the jellyfish out of the way—" "That usually takes some time," the Gryphon

18
00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:26.984
interrupted. "You take two steps forward—" "With a lobster as a partner," the Gryphon said.

19
00:01:27.752 --> 00:01:29.633
"Of course," the Mock Turtle said.

20
00:01:29.653 --> 00:01:37.958
"You step forward twice, face your partner, and—" "Change lobsters," the Gryphon said.

21
00:01:37.978 --> 00:01:45.942
"Then you throw the lobsters—" "As far out to sea as you can," the Mock Turtle said.

22
00:01:45.962 --> 00:01:49.524
"And swim after them," the Gryphon said.

23
00:01:49.544 --> 00:01:52.966
"Then do a somersault in the sea!"

24
00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:56.968
The Mock Turtle danced wildly about.

25
00:01:58.636 --> 00:02:00.618
"And change lobsters again!"

26
00:02:00.998 --> 00:02:03.200
the Gryphon yelled at the top of his lungs.

27
00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:08.144
"Go back to land again," the Mock Turtle said.

28
00:02:08.164 --> 00:02:11.947
"And the first part of the dance is over."

29
00:02:13.148 --> 00:02:16.550
Both creatures had been jumping around while they described the dance.

30
00:02:17.952 --> 00:02:20.534
Now they sat down and looked at Alice.

31
00:02:21.655 --> 00:02:23.716
She wasn't sure how to react.

32
00:02:23.736 --> 00:02:28.160
"It must be a very pretty dance," she finally said.

33
00:02:29.192 --> 00:02:31.053
"Would you like to see some of it?"

34
00:02:31.533 --> 00:02:32.613
the Mock Turtle asked.

35
00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:34.014
"Oh yes!"

36
00:02:35.315 --> 00:02:39.996
"We can do the first part without lobsters," the Mock Turtle said to the Gryphon.

37
00:02:40.016 --> 00:02:42.197
"Do you want to sing?"

38
00:02:42.217 --> 00:02:47.800
"You should sing because I've forgotten the words," the Gryphon replied.

39
00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.902
So the Mock Turtle sang about a snail doing the lobster dance.

40
00:02:59.448 --> 00:03:04.833
The two creatures began to dance around Alice, sometimes stepping on her feet by mistake.

41
00:03:08.176 --> 00:03:10.598
When they finished dancing, Alice clapped.

42
00:03:10.618 --> 00:03:18.144
"Now we want to hear about some of your adventures," the Gryphon said.

43
00:03:19.185 --> 00:03:22.388
He and the Mock Turtle sat on either side of Alice.

44
00:03:22.408 --> 00:03:30.245
"Well, if you're sure you want to hear my story First, I chased the White Rabbit and fell

45
00:03:30.285 --> 00:03:32.165
down the rabbit hole," she began.

46
00:03:33.066 --> 00:03:37.207
By the time she told them about meeting the Caterpillar, they looked bored.

47
00:03:37.227 --> 00:03:41.468
"That's enough of your story," the Gryphon said.

48
00:03:41.488 --> 00:03:43.929
"But I'm not at the end!"

49
00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:44.969
Alice said.

50
00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:48.770
Once again she thought how rude everyone was.

51
00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:53.231
"Let's try more of the lobster dance," the Gryphon said.

52
00:03:54.372 --> 00:03:55.412
He turned to Alice.

53
00:03:56.252 --> 00:03:59.173
"Or would you like the Mock Turtle to sing another song?"

54
00:03:59.193 --> 00:04:04.435
"Another song, please," Alice replied so quickly that the Gryphon frowned.

55
00:04:04.455 --> 00:04:07.736
"Well." He sniffed.

56
00:04:08.396 --> 00:04:10.077
"That's not what I'd have chosen.

57
00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:14.799
But if that's what you want The Gryphon looked at the Mock Turtle.

58
00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:18.460
"Sing 'Turtle Soup' for her, old fellow."

59
00:04:19.776 --> 00:04:25.020
The Mock Turtle sighed and began to sing a song in a voice choked with sobs.

60
00:04:26.582 --> 00:04:31.505
He was interrupted by a voice calling, "The trial's beginning!"

61
00:04:31.525 --> 00:04:33.647
"Come on!"

62
00:04:33.887 --> 00:04:34.728
the Gryphon cried.

63
00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:39.972
Without waiting for the Mock Turtle, he grabbed Alice by the hand and ran off.

64
00:04:39.992 --> 00:04:41.774
"Whose trial is it?"

65
00:04:42.134 --> 00:04:42.814
Alice asked.

66
00:04:43.615 --> 00:04:46.417
But the Gryphon only repeated, "Come on!"

67
00:04:48.339 --> 00:04:49.480
and ran faster.
